  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 17A—Protected international trade marks under the Madrid Protocol",
    "Division 2—Application for international registration of a trade mark",
    "17A.6  Eligibility to apply for international registration"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "17A.6",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r17A.6",
  "text": "(1) A person who is: (a) the registered owner of a registered trade mark; or (b) an applicant for registration of a trade mark; may apply for international registration of the trade mark. (2) The person must: (a) be an Australian citizen; or (b) be domiciled in Australia; or (c) have a real and effective industrial or commercial establishment in Australia. Note: These requirements are stated in Article 2(1)(ii) of the Protocol. (3) Two or more persons may jointly apply for international registration of a trade mark as allowed by rule 8 of the Madrid Regulations.",
  "title": "Eligibility to apply for international registration",
